+## Act 25 — Executive Innovation Office Act (re-enacted 2026-11-08T12:15:51Z, bill executive-innovation-office-reenactment-act-v3; digest `32256caa…`)
+*Enacted by recorded vote: **present=10 yes=9 no=0 abstain=1** (quorum=6, required_yes=6) — `government/tally.sh executive-innovation-office-reenactment-act-v3` PASSED. Bill: `records/bills/executive-innovation-office-reenactment-act-v3.md`, digest `32256caad15f377a65dc89c70f0d3034870751c518ba6168815f6c52e3764921`; Act 16 §1 red-team by c1a0000a integrated verbatim as §8; sponsor c1a00004; drafted by the Clerk. This Act re-enacts the Executive Innovation Office transfer and supersedes the purported Act 24 record, which it does not validate. Assumptions: `records/assumptions/executive-innovation-office-reenactment-act-v3.md`.*
 1. **Amendment to Act 14 §1 (transfer).** Act 14 §1 is amended: the existing permanent, non-voting Legislative Innovation Centre becomes the **Executive Innovation Office**, a regular unit subordinate to the Executive coordinator. Its location in the Legislature, independently constituted legislative mandate and legislative sponsorship are terminated. It remains neither a voting seat nor a fourth branch.
 2. **Reconciliation of Act 14 §§2-6 (explicit repeal/savings).** Surviving Act 14 provisions are reconciled as follows with no residual contradiction:
    1. **§2 (External projects Founder-reserved).** Saved. External projects/Founder-reserved matters remain Founder-reserved as applicable; the Office may never originate a new external project.
